-This is not an official Google product.
+# SyzPilot-Fuzzer
+
+ML-guided directed kernel fuzzing — Fuzzer (CPU) side. Modified Syzkaller with reachability filtering, guided syscall selection, and template-guided mutation.
+
+## Introduction
+
+SyzPilot-fuzzer is a modified version of [syzkaller](https://github.com/google/syzkaller) that integrates ML-guided directed fuzzing. It communicates with SyzPilot-Brain for model training and guidance, and uses local inference to schedule program execution toward target kernel code.
+
+The patch distributed with SyzPilot targets upstream syzkaller commit
+`6e83b42dcfcd13c3b8e0d5c803cdcc424c0fbff9`. The historical import that
+started this repository omitted 31 upstream-only files, including GitHub
+metadata and canned manager-config test fixtures. Applying the patch to the
+complete upstream checkout retains those files; the patch must be validated
+against that checkout before use. In the historical imported tree alone,
+`pkg/mgrconfig.TestCanned` fails because its `testdata/*.cfg` fixtures are
+missing; it passes with the complete upstream fixtures. This repository is
+licensed under Apache 2.0.
+
+**Key features**:
+- **Reachability filtering** (rfilter) — async ML-based scheduling (skip/smash/pass)
+- **Guided syscall selection** — 30% bias toward target-relevant syscalls
+- **Template-guided mutation** — inserts guidance-provided syscall sequences with argument constraints
+- **Training data collection** — streams labeled programs to Brain via gRPC
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                    syz-manager                               │
+│                                                              │
+│  Registration ──► Brain Controller                           │
+│  OnModelReady ──► EnableRFSource()                           │
+│  OnGuidance ──► ApplyGuidance()                              │
+│                                                              │
+│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
+│  │                    Fuzzer                            │    │
+│  │  ReachFilterSource (async inference pipeline)        │    │
+│  │  GuidedChoiceTable (30% guided selection)            │    │
+│  │  templateInsert (template-guided mutation)           │    │
+│  │  DataCollector (gRPC streaming to Brain)             │    │
+│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+## Installation
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+- Go 1.24.8+
+- Docker (syzpilot-fuzzer container)
+- Linux kernel with KCOV support
+- QEMU for VM-based fuzzing
+
+### Build
+
+The fuzzer **must** be compiled inside the `syzpilot-fuzzer` Docker container:
+
+```bash
+docker exec syzpilot-fuzzer bash -lc '
+  export go_version=1.24.8
+  export GOPATH=~/software/gopath-common
+  export GOROOT=~/software/go$go_version
+  export PATH=$GOROOT/bin:$PATH:$GOPATH/bin
+  cd /root/SyzPilot-fuzzer && make -j$(nproc)
+'
+```
+
+Binary: `bin/syz-manager`
+
+### Directory Layout (inside container)
+
+```
+/root/SyzPilot-fuzzer/          # This repository (bind-mounted from host)
+/root/kernels/                  # Compiled kernels (bind-mounted from host)
+/root/images-auto/image-{1..5}/ # VM images (5 copies for parallel load)
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Plain Fuzzing (no Brain or target observation)
+
+This mode rejects `/guidance` even if a client posts to the Manager's HTTP
+endpoint. Standalone oracle/ablation guidance requires an explicit
+`"allow_standalone_guidance": true` in the `SyzPilot` object; never set it
+for a feature-off baseline or a non-oracle functional comparison.
+
+```bash
+# Run the unassisted Syzkaller baseline.
+taskset -c 0-7 /root/SyzPilot-fuzzer/bin/syz-manager \
+    -config /path/to/manager.cfg -timeout 12h
+```
+
+### With Brain Registration (rfilter + guidance)
+
+Add SyzPilot config to `manager.cfg`. Replace every placeholder with a value
+for the evaluator's own kernel, VM image, network, and work directory. Resolve
+target PCs with SyzPilot's `analyzer/get_targets.py` (using
+`function@source-file:line`), rather than copying addresses from another
+kernel build. The Docker bridge address is host-dependent.
+
+```json
+{
+  "SyzPilot": {
+    "task_name": "<report-derived bug title>",
+    "network_mode": "isolated",
+    "enable_dump": true,
+    "dump_dir": "<absolute per-run output directory>",
+    "target_pcs": ["<resolved PC 1>", "<resolved PC 2>"],
+    "reach_filter": {
+      "enable": true,
+      "controller": "<reachable Brain host>:<Controller port>"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+```bash
+taskset -c 0-7 /root/SyzPilot-fuzzer/bin/syz-manager \
+    -config /path/to/manager.cfg -timeout 12h \
+    -bench /path/to/bench.log
+```
+
+### Oracle-only PoC diagnostic (excluded from Functional evaluation)
+
+The HTTP guidance endpoint can accept PoC-derived templates for an offline
+oracle diagnostic. Such templates use target information unavailable to the
+normal fuzzer. Do **not** inject a target PoC or reproducer in the artifact's
+Functional workflow or in a directed-fuzzing comparison. Normal guidance is
+derived from the target report and static analysis, then refined from online
+coverage and model attribution.
+
+For an explicitly labeled oracle diagnostic only:
+
+Set `"SyzPilot": {"allow_standalone_guidance": true}` in that run's
+`manager.cfg` before posting; the ordinary feature-off baseline must leave it
+false. This opt-in is unnecessary when reach filtering is enabled.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:<HTTP_PORT>/guidance \
+    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+    -d @/path/to/poc_guidance.json
+```
+
+## Configuration Reference
+
+### SyzPilot Config (in manager.cfg)
+
+| Field | Type | Default | Description |
+|-------|------|---------|-------------|
+| `task_name` | string | "" | Bug title or patch commit |
+| `network_mode` | string | "isolated" | "isolated" (SSH tunnel) or "direct" |
+| `enable_dump` | bool | false | Dump programs and coverage |
+| `observe_target_coverage` | bool | false | Collect target-PC statistics and final-hit evidence without Brain, training, rfilter, or guidance; use for measurement-matched feature-off controls |
+| `allow_standalone_guidance` | bool | false | Accept HTTP guidance without reach filtering only for explicitly labeled oracle/ablation runs; never use for a feature-off baseline |
+| `dump_dir` | string | "SyzPilot-default-dumpdir" | Dump directory path; observation-only controls require an explicit absolute per-instance path |
+| `target_pcs` | []string | [] | Target PC addresses (32-bit hex) |
+| `cold_start_seed_dir` | string | "" | Directory containing generic generated seed programs; must be paired with `cold_start_seed_catalog` |
+| `cold_start_seed_catalog` | string | "" | Versioned catalog authenticating eligible generic `NoGenerate` seeds for the exact compiled target |
+| `cold_start_auto_dependencies` | bool | false | Add a minimum static resource-constructor closure for authenticated seeds; added calls become normal fuzzing candidates |
+| `directed_corpus.enable` | bool | false | Opt into a bounded runtime-only pool of authenticated seeds and waypoint-reaching programs; requires target PCs and a guidance path |
+| `directed_corpus.capacity` | int | 256 | Maximum directed programs retained in memory (1--4096) |
+| `directed_corpus.mutation_probability` | float | 0.20 | Probability that an ordinary mutation request starts from the directed pool |
+| `directed_corpus.anchor_preserve_probability` | float | 0.95 | Probability that a directed mutation retains at least one preferred syscall already present in its source |
+| `template_insert_weight` | int | 50 | Sequence-template mutation weight; 0 disables template insertion |
+| `reach_filter.enable` | bool | false | Enable rfilter |
+| `reach_filter.controller` | string | "" | Brain controller address (ip:port) |
+| `reach_filter.bsize` | int | 16 | Inference batch size |
+| `scheduling_strategy.type` | int | 3 | 1=skip only, 2=+smash, 3=+time decay |
+| `scheduling_strategy.alpha` | float | 0.6 | Skip probability scaling |
+| `scheduling_strategy.beta` | float | 0.5 | Probability curve shape |
+| `scheduling_strategy.lambda` | float | 0.03 | Time decay rate (per hour) |
+
+### HTTP Endpoints
+
+| Endpoint | Method | Description |
+|----------|--------|-------------|
+| `/` | GET | Fuzzer dashboard |
+| `/api/stats` | GET | Execution statistics JSON |
+| `/api/task` | GET | Task information |
+| `/model_ready` | POST | Callback from Brain (model deployed) |
+| `/guidance` | POST | Callback from Brain (guidance update) |
+
+### Generic `NoGenerate` cold-start seeds
+
+Some syzlang calls are marked `NoGenerate`: they cannot be chosen by normal
+random generation, but trusted programs containing them may still be executed
+and mutated. SyzPilot keeps the native candidate and corpus paths unchanged. If
+Brain recommends one of these calls, the manager may additionally enqueue the
+matching generic `syz-imagegen` programs as minimized candidates.
+
+Both `cold_start_seed_dir` and `cold_start_seed_catalog` are required to enable
+this path. The checked-in Linux/amd64 catalog is bound to the compiled syzlang
+target revision and records each seed's SHA-256 digest, `requires: manual`
+provenance, and exact `NoGenerate` calls. The manager rejects stale, modified,
+symlinked, or structurally invalid assets. It never scans target reports, PoCs,
+reproducers, corpus databases, or arbitrary user files.
+
+Regenerate the catalog after changing syzlang descriptions or generated tests:
+
+```bash
+make syzpilot-seed-catalog
+./bin/syzpilot-seed-catalog \
+    -os linux -arch amd64 \
+    -seed-dir sys/linux/test \
+    -output syz-manager/syzpilot_seed_catalog_linux_amd64.json
+```
+
+The catalog records one deterministic representative for every
+canonical-unique eligible generated program rather than naming a filesystem or
+syscall family in code. Coverage is intentionally bounded by the generic assets
+shipped with the pinned Syzkaller tree; a recommended `NoGenerate` call without
+such an asset receives no seed injection and native fuzzing continues normally.
+
+The optional `directed_corpus` is additive and disabled by default. Enabling it
+does not change native candidate ordering, native signal-based corpus admission,
+or `corpus.db`. Authenticated cold-start seeds are copied into a bounded
+runtime-only pool, and a successfully completed execution is also retained when
+its KCOV trace explicitly contains at least one configured target PC. An
+overflowed trace may contribute an observed positive target but never a
+negative or shallow training label. Directed entries feed the same
+`MutateWithOpts` path as native corpus programs and can participate in normal
+splicing and collision. Anchor preservation is syscall-presence preservation,
+not argument freezing: by default 95% of selected directed mutations retry or
+fall back until at least one current guidance anchor remains, while 5% accept
+the ordinary mutator result so an incorrect anchor does not become permanent.
+
+## Architecture Details
+
+### ReachFilterSource (rfilter)
+
+Async producer-consumer pattern:
+- One background inference worker batches pending prediction requests via TorchServe gRPC
+- `Next()` waits for its request's decision while the original queue retains ownership
+- Whitelisted queues (triage, candidate) bypass prediction; malformed or unavailable predictions fail open
+- Time decay reduces filtering aggressiveness over the campaign
+
+### GuidedChoiceTable
+
+Extends syzkaller's ChoiceTable:
+- 30% chance of guided selection when guidance data exists
+- Of the remaining 70%, 5% are random and 95% use corpus-based priority
+- Effective proportions with guidance are 30% guided, 3.5% random, and 66.5% corpus-based
+
+### Template Insertion
+
+Mutation strategy that inserts guidance-provided syscall sequences:
+- Select template weighted by priority
+- Resolve syscall names, generate calls
+- Apply ArgConstraint hints (fixed argument values)
+- Insert as prefix, suffix, or replace
+
+### Data Collector
+
+gRPC bidirectional streaming to Brain:
+- Samples balanced at 10:1 negative:positive ratio
+- Auto-flush at 100 samples or 5-minute interval
+- Automatic reconnection on errors
+- The release configuration syncs the active-buffer WAL for each accepted
+  sample; a return from the Collector therefore preserves its durable tail.
+- Template mutation outcomes are exported to `-bench` as aggregate counters:
+  attempts, succeeded, unavailable, no capacity, generation failed,
+  constraint failed, and too large. `succeeded` means that the mutation
+  operator inserted the generated call closure into a program; it does not by
+  itself prove that the program executed or reached a target.
+
+## Debugging
+
+### Check fuzzer status
+
+```bash
+# All groups at a glance
+docker exec syzpilot-fuzzer bash -lc "
+for d in /root/experiments/case_N_*/*/; do
+    name=\$(basename \$(dirname \$d))/\$(basename \$d)
+    last=\$(tail -1 \$d/fuzzer.log 2>/dev/null)
+    echo \"\$name: \$last\"
+done"
+
+# Crashes for a group
+docker exec syzpilot-fuzzer bash -lc "
+for d in /root/experiments/case_N_GROUP/crashes/*/; do
+    cat \$d/description 2>/dev/null
+done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn"
+```
+
+### Check Brain connectivity
+
+```bash
+curl -fsS "$BRAIN_URL/health"
+```
+
+Set `BRAIN_URL` to the controller URL reachable from the fuzzer container;
+its address depends on the evaluator's Docker network.
+
+### Debug logger
+
+When `enable_debug: true` in config, detailed logs are written to `<workdir>/debuglogger.log`.
+
+## Related Repositories
+
+| Repository | Purpose |
+|------------|---------|
+| SyzPilot | Brain-side controller and ML pipeline (Python) |
+| KallGraph-full | Static analysis for indirect call analysis (C++) |
